## Context

- Co-presenting an OpenClaw seminar in April 2026, covering Windows installation and a Skills-based research digest demo.
- Regular collaborators: James, Wenrui, Jiahao.

## Research interests

- Mechanistic interpretability — understanding how transformer language models compute internally, via circuit analysis, attention-head studies, and feature visualization.
- LLM agents and tool use — planning, function calling, and multi-step reasoning in agent frameworks; evaluation of agent capabilities in realistic tasks.
- Parameter-efficient fine-tuning — low-rank adaptation, adapter methods, and prompt tuning techniques that avoid full model retraining.
- Retrieval-augmented generation — how retrieval improves factual grounding in LLMs, including long-context retrieval and hybrid dense-sparse strategies.

## Explicit non-interests

- Pure computer vision work without a language or multimodal connection.
- Hardware and systems papers without machine-learning relevance.
- Pure theory papers without empirical grounding.

